# PR stacking and catalog files

`docs/remaining-work.md`, `docs/features.md`, and `docs/todo/HISTORY.md` are
merge magnets. Parallel PRs that all rewrite the same leftovers table or feature
bullet will conflict even when the product code is independent.

## Catalog edits

- While implementing: status lives only in `docs/todo/<task>.md` (and a worklog
  only if that session still has open follow-ups).
- Do **not** edit `docs/remaining-work.md`, `docs/features.md`, or
  `docs/todo/HISTORY.md` on intermediate commits.
- When the PR is otherwise ready to merge (code, tests, lint/format): fold
  catalogs in **one** commit — append HISTORY, strip shipped rows from
  remaining-work, update `features.md` if the product surface changed.
- After merge, delete the todo/worklog as in `todo-history.mdc`.
- Do not start a session by rewriting those catalogs. If `docs/todo/` still
  contains already-shipped files, fold them only in a ready-to-merge commit,
  not as a drive-by on an unrelated branch.

## Stack related PRs

- If work shares files, a todo list, or a feature area (e.g. MOB-01 then MOB-04
  then MOB-09), branch B from A. Do not open parallel PRs from `main` that will
  all rewrite the same catalogs or the same test `describe`.
- Unrelated work may stay parallel **if** it skips catalog edits until each PR
  is ready, then rebases onto `main` after a sibling lands.
- Prefer a new test file over appending to a shared `describe` that another
  open PR is also editing.

## Do not

- Merge `main` into every open PR on every sibling land as a substitute for
  stacking. That relocates the conflict; it does not prevent it.
- Open many PRs from slightly different `main`s for slices of one audit.
